            <ArticleTitle>Acute acalculous cholecystitis in a child returning from the Ivory Coast.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>242-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute cholecystitis is an uncommon occurrence in children. Acute acalculous cholecystitis (AAC) has various etiology; among them are a wide variety of infectious agents. We report the case of a 7-year-old child who presented AAC due to plasmodium falciparum infection. The causes of AAC are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
